\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Chemistry 1015 1 minute 8 seconds\cb1 \
\cb3 OK, so...\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Chemistry 1015 1 minute 10 seconds\cb1 \
\cb3 We'll cover the when to use it, we'll cover the how to use it, and we'll cover just briefly the why to use it.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Chemistry 1015 1 minute 21 seconds\cb1 \
\cb3 So first of all, the wedding.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Chemistry 1015 1 minute 31 seconds\cb1 \
\cb3 So there's three conditions that have to be present. All 3 have to be present for you to use the FPC. The first is if you're sampling from a finite population.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Chemistry 1015 2 minutes 2 seconds\cb1 \
\cb3 So how will you know you're working with a finite population in a question? Well, they'll actually give you the size of the population. So the size will be something like 2000, which is definitely finite.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Chemistry 1015 2 minutes 18 seconds\cb1 \
\cb3 Okay.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Chemistry 1015 2 minutes 21 seconds\cb1 \
\cb3 Then the second thing that has to hold is that the sampling has to be done.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Chemistry 1015 2 minutes 28 seconds\cb1 \
\cb3 Without replacement.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Chemistry 1015 2 minutes 35 seconds\cb1 \
\cb3 So once something is sampled, it is completely removed from the...\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Chemistry 1015 2 minutes 41 seconds\cb1 \
\cb3 Potential pool for sampling.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Chemistry 1015 2 minutes 44 seconds\cb1 \
\cb3 And it cannot be sampled again. Sampling with replacement means that it can be sampled again.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Chemistry 1015 2 minutes 57 seconds\cb1 \
\cb3 And then the final condition is that the proportion of your sample to your population size, so the size of the sample as a proportion of the size of the population, must exceed 0.05, in other words, 5%.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Chemistry 1015 3 minutes 20 seconds\cb1 \
\cb3 So, this signifies...\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
